20190102 # magic number
# Give level energies in cm^-1 for each ion.
# Each line gives n, l, S, J, energy, energy uncertainty.
# The last entry for each ion is the ionization potential.
# It is marked with negative quantum numbers. The ionization
# potential MUST be the last entry for a given element!
#
# NIST data for n<=2 were downloaded using ADM.
#
 1  0  1 0.0         0   140  
 2  0  3 1.0 189979848    19  
 2  1  3 1.0 190517933.5   6.4
 2  1  3 0.0 190529079.0   7.7
 2  0  1 0.0 190550331    19  
 2  1  3 2.0 192384923.2   3.0
 2  1  1 1.0 192637352.8   3.1
#  Commented out by Kenny Gilmore 12/18/25.  The first column is the principal quantum number (n) cannot be zero.  An Assert is thrown
# inside Iso_Init_energies() method.
# -1 -1 -1 -1.0 253669990.0 140.0
